---
name: Note Writer
description: Turns a meeting transcript into a published note with stored provenance.
session: shared
base_dir: __PROJECT_DIR__
accepts:
- transcript.ready
tools:
- read
- query_content
- transform_content
- finish
---
A meeting transcript is available at {{ event.payload.path }}.

Build a published note from it using ONLY the content tools, so every
derived value keeps its provenance. Follow these steps exactly, one tool
call at a time. Every `transform_content` response returns the new `head`
to use as `expected_head` in the next call.

1. Call `read` on `{{ event.payload.path }}`.

2. Call `query_content` with `{}`. Note the returned `head`.

3. Call `transform_content` to store the transcript verbatim:
   - `expected_head`: the head from step 2
   - `reason`: "store source transcript"
   - `inputs`: `{}`
   - `transformation`: `{"type": "literal", "title": "Meeting transcript", "value": <the exact, complete text of the transcript file, unchanged>}`
   - `destination`: `{"key": "transcript", "kind": "document", "scope": "run", "expected_object_id": null}`

4. Call `transform_content` to derive the summary with a model call:
   - `expected_head`: the head returned by step 3
   - `reason`: "summarize transcript"
   - `inputs`: `{"keys": ["transcript"]}`
   - `transformation`: `{"type": "model", "mode": "one", "instruction": "Summarize this meeting transcript in exactly two sentences."}`
   - `destination`: `{"key": "summary", "kind": "text", "scope": "run", "expected_object_id": null}`

5. Call `transform_content` to derive the published note:
   - `expected_head`: the head returned by step 4
   - `reason`: "write published note"
   - `inputs`: `{"keys": ["summary"]}`
   - `transformation`: `{"type": "model", "mode": "one", "instruction": "Rewrite this summary as one sentence suitable for a public status page."}`
   - `destination`: `{"key": "note", "kind": "text", "scope": "run", "expected_object_id": null}`
   The response's `object_ids` contains the note's object id.

6. Call `finish` with `{"object_id": <the note object id from step 5>}`.

Never write files. Never paraphrase or summarize the content yourself in a
message; only the model transformations in steps 4 and 5 may produce
derived text.
